  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,1})+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(X=2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.70-0.40 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
